course: dictionary
lesson: 12615
title: Discretion: knowing when to be careful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Discretion is a noun. It means being careful about what you say and do, especially when someone could be hurt, upset or let down. «Mia kept the surprise party a secret and showed great discretion.» She did not spoil the plan, because she knew it would hurt the surprise.
explain: Discretion can also mean the freedom to decide. «The class trip is at the teacher's discretion.» Here the word means the teacher can choose what happens. Ask yourself: is someone being careful, or is someone allowed to choose? The words around it tell you which.
explain: You may also see discretion in a formal warning: «Viewer discretion advised.» It means take care, because some things may upset you. Read the whole sentence and the clue will be there.
fact: Discretion is a noun.
fact: «Discretion» can mean being careful not to tell secrets or upset people.
fact: «Discretion» can also mean the freedom to decide, as in «at the teacher's discretion».
fact: «Viewer discretion advised» is a formal warning that some things may upset you, so take care.
exercise: «Mia kept the surprise party a secret. She showed great discretion.» What does discretion mean here? | Telling everyone in the class at once | *Being careful not to tell secrets or upset people | Running away from the party | Choosing a new colour for the cake
exercise: «The class trip is at the teacher's discretion.» What does discretion mean here? | The trip is cancelled for ever | *The teacher has the freedom to decide | The teacher must pay for everyone's trip | The class must vote on every detail
exercise: A TV warning says «Viewer discretion advised.» What does it warn you about? | The show is very funny | The show is about cooking | The show has no sound | *Some things may upset you, so take care
test: «Tom did not tell anyone about Sam's secret. He showed discretion.» What does discretion mean? | *Being careful not to share a secret | Shouting loudly in class | Forgetting what happened | Telling everyone in the playground
test: «The head teacher will decide the new rule, at her discretion.» What does at her discretion mean? | It is written in a book | *It is her choice to decide | It has been stopped | It will happen tomorrow
exam: Ava reads «Viewer discretion advised» before a film. What does it mean? | The film will be very long | The film is free to watch | The film is in colour | *Take care, some scenes may upset you
